 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Gradient Clipping:** Colors are not clipped to $[0,1]$ during training to avoid zeroing gradients for pixels marginally above one, which can cause issues with white walls/sky [S2, unofficial]. Clipping is only applied during inference [S2, unofficial].
-*   **SH Degree Progression:** Only $0^{th}$ degree SH is used initially. Higher degrees are enabled every 1000 iterations [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Opacity Learning Rate:** Using $\eta_\alpha = 0.05$ (original) creates more Gaussians than $\eta_\alpha = 0.025$ (official), which yields cleaner reconstructions with fewer Gaussians [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Gradient Clipping:** Clipping colors to $[0,1]$ during training sets gradients to zero for pixels marginally above one, which may cause unexpected behavior with white scenes. The original approach clips only during inference [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Opacity Learning Rate:** Using a higher opacity learning rate ($0.05$) creates more Gaussians; halving it to $0.025$ yields cleaner reconstructions with fewer primitives [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Scene Extent:** The threshold for splitting depends on the scene extent $E_{scene}$. Incorrect estimation leads to over-splitting or under-splitting [S2, unofficial][S3].
